id: pm-rlm-sr0b
title: Align empty response checkpoint validation with engine recovery
description: "GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/issues/5. The engine writes empty string responses as billable invalid-action refusals, while the loader rejects them as incomplete. Accept every engine-written response state while rejecting non-string values. Prove completed replay/resume and interrupted recovery on real SDK trackers."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T00:39:09.718Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T02:37:00.740Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "Empty, whitespace and malformed JSON string responses survive completed and interrupted recovery; non-string persisted responses remain incomplete refusals; regression fails when loader fix is reverted."
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T00:47:30.607Z",codex-agent,"Issue 5 reproduced before the fix: both completed and interrupted empty-response regressions failed with incomplete from load. Cause: the writer accepts every string, while the loader used nonempty text validation. Loader now accepts empty strings, preserving recorded invalid-action refusals and rejecting non-string values. Focused controls for malformed JSON and whitespace pass, completed resume performs no inference, and interrupted recovery reuses its pending reservation."
  "2026-10-19T00:55:34.080Z",codex-agent,"Revert evidence: restoring only nonempty response-text validation makes both completed empty-response replay and interrupted empty-response recovery fail their assertions. The real-SDK suite also preserves rejection of non-string responses and malformed settlement markers. The package-wide proof runner passed 24/24 with exact source hash restoration; the issue-linked pm test run passed 1/1 command (2/2 tests)."
